[
  {
    "index": 0,
    "startSeconds": 0.0,
    "endSeconds": 2.48,
    "text": "The Kaabu Empire is gone.",
    "charStart": 0,
    "charEnd": 25
  },
  {
    "index": 1,
    "startSeconds": 2.48,
    "endSeconds": 6.12,
    "text": "Its capitals are ruins in the bush of Guinea-Bissau.",
    "charStart": 27,
    "charEnd": 79
  },
  {
    "index": 2,
    "startSeconds": 6.12,
    "endSeconds": 8.09,
    "text": "Its warriors are dust.",
    "charStart": 80,
    "charEnd": 102
  },
  {
    "index": 3,
    "startSeconds": 8.09,
    "endSeconds": 15.18,
    "text": "Its royal lineages are dispersed across West Africa, known now only to those who have kept the genealogies.",
    "charStart": 103,
    "charEnd": 210
  },
  {
    "index": 4,
    "startSeconds": 15.18,
    "endSeconds": 18.27,
    "text": "But Kelefa Saane is not gone.",
    "charStart": 212,
    "charEnd": 241
  },
  {
    "index": 5,
    "startSeconds": 18.27,
    "endSeconds": 28.54,
    "text": "Every time a kora is tuned, every time a jali opens his throat and begins — I ko Kelefa, I ko Kelefa — the warrior-prince of Kaabu is alive again.",
    "charStart": 243,
    "charEnd": 389
  },
  {
    "index": 6,
    "startSeconds": 28.54,
    "endSeconds": 30.62,
    "text": "In the vibration of the strings.",
    "charStart": 390,
    "charEnd": 422
  },
  {
    "index": 7,
    "startSeconds": 30.62,
    "endSeconds": 34.17,
    "text": "In the silence between the notes.",
    "charStart": 423,
    "charEnd": 456
  },
  {
    "index": 8,
    "startSeconds": 34.17,
    "endSeconds": 39.11,
    "text": "In the listening.",
    "charStart": 457,
    "charEnd": 474
  },
  {
    "index": 9,
    "startSeconds": 39.11,
    "endSeconds": 43.47,
    "text": "This is what the oral tradition does that no archive can replicate.",
    "charStart": 476,
    "charEnd": 543
  },
  {
    "index": 10,
    "startSeconds": 43.47,
    "endSeconds": 44.92,
    "text": "It does not preserve information.",
    "charStart": 545,
    "charEnd": 578
  },
  {
    "index": 11,
    "startSeconds": 44.92,
    "endSeconds": 50.3,
    "text": "It preserves presence.",
    "charStart": 579,
    "charEnd": 601
  },
  {
    "index": 12,
    "startSeconds": 50.3,
    "endSeconds": 51.74,
    "text": "Gordon Innes, the scholar who spent years recording and translating the Kelefaba in the 1970s, understood this.",
    "charStart": 603,
    "charEnd": 714
  },
  {
    "index": 13,
    "startSeconds": 51.74,
    "endSeconds": 61.43,
    "text": "He wrote that the griots were not merely entertainers or historians — they were the living memory of a people, and their performances were acts of resurrection.",
    "charStart": 715,
    "charEnd": 875
  },
  {
    "index": 14,
    "startSeconds": 61.43,
    "endSeconds": 67.7,
    "text": "Every night a griot performs the Kelefaba, Kelefa crosses the river again.",
    "charStart": 877,
    "charEnd": 951
  },
  {
    "index": 15,
    "startSeconds": 67.7,
    "endSeconds": 73.15,
    "text": "And in crossing it, he reminds us what it means to live without flinching.",
    "charStart": 953,
    "charEnd": 1027
  }
]